{"authored" [{"question" "q-13807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0fe9e8494485603aa2f1a0d0e2a29d59ad83a7b6f14b22479a6b3e533506f8e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-13807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}\\cdot  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0fe9e8494485603aa2f1a0d0e2a29d59ad83a7b6f14b22479a6b3e533506f8e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-13807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5" "basis" 1138 "verification" "