ake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0fe9e8494485603aa2f1a0d0e2a29d59ad83a7b6f14b22479a6b3e533506f8e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-13803" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0fe9e8494485603aa2f1a0d0e2a29d59ad83a7b6f14b22479a6b3e533506f8e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0fe9e8494485603aa2f1a0d0e2a29d59ad83a7b6f14b22479a6b3e533506f8e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0fe9e8494485603aa2f1a0d0e2a29d59ad83a7b6f14b22479a6b3e533506f8e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "222fe31908a93b53786ab4aa511ab10b01045386db1a176ffaba2a0d129ce6d5" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0fe9e8494485603aa2f1a0d0e2a29d59ad83a7b6f14b22479a6b3e533506f8e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14405.json" "file_sha256" "2cc85fe9c460f9351375a20b0c5d037ab2482bb1b0648d80857a1becb926c86e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14405.json" "file_sha256" "2cc85fe9c460f9351375a20b0c5d037ab2482bb1b0648d80857a1becb926c86e" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14406.json" "file_sha256" "dbe57670314d8113b536dd73dc121fd43b6e0852c3e160722b325ffd71c116a3" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2 }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3({log}_{3}⁡x)^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14406.json" "file_sha256" "dbe57670314d8113b536dd73dc121fd43b6e0852c3e160722b325ffd71c116a3" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14422.json" "file_sha256" "278fdc27dc2aa71e3861bbf0a0d4ba2d2007ce8fd5062f66273f8922f6ca72a0" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n&= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}\\[5pt]\n&=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n&=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2}\\[5pt] \n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{7}{3}\t\t\n\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/example-14422.json" "file_sha256" "278fdc27dc2aa71e3861bbf0a0d4ba2d2007ce8fd5062f66273f8922f6ca72a0" "basis" 1138 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009028/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{2}{x{log}_{5}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/state.json" "file_sha256" "a327107e917adda7c7748e617fca468d99eec5fb29bfa4fe429923a8398cafeb" "basis" 1193 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{5}⁡(3x).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x{log}_{5}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{{log}_{5}⁡(3x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{5}⁡(3x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/state.json" "file_sha256" "a327107e917adda7c7748e617fca468d99eec5fb29bfa4fe429923a8398cafeb" "basis" 1193 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture"