 above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{5}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{5}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-31394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c423bfc653e06a330fcb95a0f17433b4888dfe6f20bc47c1eac6303ac7ef1edc"} {"question" "q-31394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-31394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{5}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{5}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{5}^{2}⁡x}{x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-31394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{5}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-49606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-49606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | ${e}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-49606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c423bfc653e06a330fcb95a0f17433b4888dfe6f20bc47c1eac6303ac7ef1edc"} {"question" "q-49606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-49606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-49606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-31619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e/5}^{{e}^{4}/5}\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-31619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x).$ Then  we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5x}\\cdot 5=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e/5$ | ${e}^{4}/5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e/5}^{{e}^{4}/5}\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{e/5}^{{e}^{4}/5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{1/2}}{1/2}|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {\\sqrt{u}|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6(\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-31619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c423bfc653e06a330fcb95a0f17433b4888dfe6f20bc47c1eac6303ac7ef1edc"} {"question" "q-31619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-31619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{15}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-31619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-73653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{4{log}_{4}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-73653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{4}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{4{log}_{4}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{1}^{4}{log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡4{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-73653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c423bfc653e06a330fcb95a0f17433b4888dfe6f20bc47c1eac6303ac7ef1edc"} {"question" "q-73653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-73653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "48"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "{ln}^{2}⁡2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-73653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-351281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{e/5}^{{e}^{4}/5}\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-351281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5x}\\cdot 5=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e/5$ | ${e}^{4}/5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e/5}^{{e}^{4}/5}\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{e/5}^{{e}^{4}/5}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-351281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c423bfc653e06a330fcb95a0f17433b4888dfe6f20bc47c1eac6303ac7ef1edc"} {"question" "q-351281" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-351281" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(4)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-73656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{8}^{64}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{8}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-73656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{8}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡8\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $8$ | $64$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{8}^{64}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{8}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{8}^{64}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{8}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡8\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡8{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡8(2\\sqrt{u}){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡8(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =2(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-73656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c423bfc653e06a330fcb95a0f17433b4888dfe6f20bc47c1eac6303ac7ef1edc"} {"question" "q-73656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-73656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(1-\\sqrt{2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡8"] ["math" "2(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡8"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡8"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "q-73656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/state.json" "file_sha256" "d32a102433672e84143541a133d44b6ff3ca7625b16d6ca3de809fd6ed9c52ce"} {"question" "e-14405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/example-14405.json" "file_sha256" "ac63e4234d1682122a45d37e80998af77a0809cef193725f094fd4e90a120e8d"} {"question" "e-14405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/example-14405.json" "file_sha256" "ac63e4234d1682122a45d37e80998af77a0809cef193725f094fd4e90a120e8d"} {"question" "e-14406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/example-14406.json" "file_sha256" "583f1c4029acd513df934d01534eca91f7a39b943b22ee5b1b00ed8eb24475ef"} {"question" "e-14406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2 }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3({log}_{3}⁡x)^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/example-14406.json" "file_sha256" "583f1c4029acd513df934d01534eca91f7a39b943b22ee5b1b00ed8eb24475ef"} {"question" "e-14422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/example-14422.json" "file_sha256" "296b398fd9e6649645483efd8cd754d4274f859795b4b57b6ead28aed28664f0"} {"question" "e-14422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n&= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}\\[5pt]\n&=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n&=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2}\\[5pt] \n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{7}{3}\t\t\n\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042968/example-14422.json" "file_sha256" "296b398fd9e6649645483efd8cd754d4274f859795b4b57b6ead28aed28664f0"}] "usage" {"q-13807" [] "e-14422" [] "q-210746" [] "e-14406" [] "q-73653" [] "q-31329" [] "q-114020" [] "e-14405" [] "q-31402" [] "q-13803" [] "q-73659" []} "basis" 1586 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186099339 17592186099340 17592186099341 17592186099342 17592186099343 17592186100261 17592186100262 17592186100263 17592186100264 17592186100265 17592186288891 17592186288892 17592186288893 17592186288894 17592186288895 17592186288898 17592186288899 17592186288900 17592186288901 17592186288902 17592186292396 17592186292397 17592186292398 17592186292399 17592186292400 17592186302154 17592186302155 17592186302156 17592186302157 17592186302158 1759218